WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Sugar made in a leaf must reach the roots,

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.180
growing tips and fruits.

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.430
Strip a ring of bark from a woody stem,
and sugar piles up above the ring.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.610
But in spring, a tree sends sugar upwards,

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.720
from storage roots to opening buds.

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:21.520
So how does a plant send sugar up to its
buds and down to its roots at the same

7
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.730
time?

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.510
In this mission, you'll meet
living tubes with no nucleus,

9
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.720
and their partner cells
packed with mitochondria.

10
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.430
Then you'll see how sugar is loaded
into those tubes, using energy.

11
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.760
Your mission: explain how a plant sends
sugar up to its buds and down to its roots

12
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.670
at once.
